1
00:05:37,142 --> 00:05:43,142
Loved for being unique. Hated for being different.

2
00:11:14,285 --> 00:11:20,285
Wilde is a drama, history film directed by Brian Gilbert.

3
00:16:51,428 --> 00:16:57,428
Oscar Wilde is a married playwright who has occasionally
indulged his weakness for male suitors.

4
00:22:28,571 --> 00:22:34,571
After much toil, Wilde debuts 'The Importance of Being Earnest' in London, and a chat at the
theatre with Lord Alfred 'Bosie' Douglas leads to a full-fledged romance.

5
00:28:05,714 --> 00:28:11,714
However, this affair leads to a legal dispute with Lord Alfred's oppressive father, the
Marquess of Queensberry, and, given the local anti-gay laws, Wilde is jailed.

6
00:33:42,857 --> 00:33:48,857
Wilde's vast intellect helps him survive until he regains his freedom.

7
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:26,000
Oscar Wilde, played by Stephen Fry.

8
00:44:57,142 --> 00:45:03,142
Lord Alfred 'Bosie' Douglas, played by Jude Law.

9
00:50:34,285 --> 00:50:40,285
Lady Speranza Wilde, played by Vanessa Redgrave.

10
00:56:11,428 --> 00:56:17,428
Constance Lloyd Wilde, played by Jennifer Ehle.

11
01:01:48,571 --> 01:01:54,571
Lady Queensberry, played by Gemma Jones.

12
01:07:25,714 --> 01:07:31,714
Lady Mount-Temple, played by Judy Parfitt.

13
01:13:02,857 --> 01:13:08,857
Wilde is a 1997 British biographical romantic
drama film directed by Brian Gilbert.

14
01:18:40,000 --> 01:18:46,000
The screenplay, written by Julian Mitchell, is based on
Richard Ellmann's 1987 biography of Oscar Wilde.

15
01:24:17,142 --> 01:24:23,142
It stars Stephen Fry in the title role, with Jude Law, Vanessa Redgrave, Jennifer Ehle, Gemma Jones,
Judy Parfitt, Michael Sheen, Zoë Wanamaker, and Tom Wilkinson in supporting roles.

16
01:29:54,285 --> 01:30:00,285
The film premiered at the 54th Venice International Film Festival on 1 September 1997, and was
theatrically released in the United Kingdom on 17 October 1997, by PolyGram Filmed Entertainment.

17
01:35:31,428 --> 01:35:37,428
It was praised for the performances of the cast, particularly that of Fry, who received
critical acclaim and a Best Actor nomination at the 56th Golden Globe Awards.

18
01:41:08,571 --> 01:41:14,571
Ehle and Wanamaker were both nominated for Best Actress in a
Supporting Role at the 51st British Academy Film Awards.

19
01:46:45,714 --> 01:46:51,714
The film explores themes of prison, coming out,
london, england, wife, biography.

20
01:52:22,857 --> 01:52:28,857
The tone is emotional.
